\name{cellucid_genes_search}
\alias{cellucid_genes_search}
\title{Search the genes}
\usage{
cellucid_genes_search(viewer, limit = 20, names, query)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{limit}{At most this many names (for a query). A whole number (at least 1). Default \code{20}, the viewer's own.}
\item{names}{Gene names to look up at once, exact in any case: genes lists those the dataset has, as it names them; lacks the rest. A vector or list of text (at least 1 character) (at least 1 item). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{query}{What is typed (give it or names). Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{genes}, \code{lacks} (Of the names asked for, those that are not genes of the dataset), \code{matches} (How many genes match in all), \code{total} (How many genes the dataset has). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
Gene names matching what is typed, best first, as the gene search box ranks them; or, given names, which of them the dataset has.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{genes.search} (Dataset). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_genes_search(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
